{%- comment -%}
  Care Guide — per gem
{%- endcomment -%}
  {%- case gem_handle -%}
    {%- when 'emerald' -%}
      <div class="gem-tab gem-tab--emerald">
        <h2>Care & Treatment</h2>
        <p>Emerald has a delicate internal structure. It is not fragile, but it is naturally more sensitive than harder stones like Sapphire. That inner life — its inclusions, its softness of glow, its living texture — is part of what makes it valuable. Mindful care keeps it stable, beautiful, and wearable for years.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Do:</strong> Clean gently with a soft cloth after wear. Use lukewarm water and a drop of mild soap occasionally. Store separately in a padded box to prevent knocks from harder stones. If professionally advised, light colourless oil maintenance may be done when appropriate.</li>
          <li><strong>Avoid:</strong> Heat, steam, sudden temperature shifts, ultrasonic cleaning, harsh chemicals, perfumes, detergents, and alcohol-based products. Remove during gym sessions, heavy physical activity, or situations where impact is likely.</li>
          <li><strong>On treatments:</strong> Light to moderate colourless oiling is a globally accepted and traditional practice for Emeralds, and it should always be fully disclosed on certification. What is never acceptable — and what we never carry — is heavy resin, polymer, wax, or glass filling disguised as quality. Visible oil seepage, suspicious clarity, or an unnaturally “perfect” appearance are all signs to look closer.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Handled gently, Emerald holds its colour, composure, and quiet brilliance for a lifetime.</p>
      </div>
