    {%- when 'blue-sapphire' -%}
      <div class="gem-tab gem-tab--blue_sapphire">
        <h2>Care & Treatment</h2>
        <p><strong>Blue Sapphire is one of the hardest gemstones in the world — Mohs 9 — which makes it naturally well-suited to daily wear. That said, mindful care keeps it at its best over years of use.</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Do: Clean gently with a soft cloth after wear. Use lukewarm water and a drop of mild soap occasionally. Store separately in a padded box away from harder stones. Ensure the setting is secure before wearing regularly.</li>
          <li>Avoid: Chemicals, perfumes, and detergents. Ultrasonic or steam cleaning. Extreme heat and prolonged direct sunlight. Remove during heavy physical activity, gym sessions, or contact sports.</li>
          <li>On treatments: Untreated Blue Sapphires are the most valuable and are strongly preferred for astrological use. Heat-treated stones are stable and acceptable when fully disclosed. What is never acceptable — and what we never carry — are glass-filled or diffusion-treated stones. These are unsuitable for astrology, compromise long-term durability, and should always be avoided. An unstable or shifting colour is a clear red flag.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
